messages:
maya: Quick heads-up — noticed the streaming pagination example in the Python and TypeScript snippets uses `cursor` but our runtime now expects `resume_token` for resume semantics. Small change but it breaks a few quickstart examples and the migration guide. Can someone patch the snippets + add a short note about backward compatibility? :eyes: 


 tom: I can take the snippets. planning to do a tiny PR that updates the param name and adds a compatibility example. Will also run the docs build. 


 tom: Proposed diff (very small):
```py
# old
for chunk in client.stream_responses(model="redwood/text-compact", cursor=cursor):
    print(chunk.text)

# new (resume_token alias)
for chunk in client.stream_responses(model="redwood/text-compact", resume_token=cursor):
    print(chunk.text)
```

```ts
// old
for await (const part of client.streamResponses({ model: 'redwood/text-compact', cursor })) {
  console.log(part.text)
}

// new
for await (const part of client.streamResponses({ model: 'redwood/text-compact', resume_token: cursor })) {
  console.log(part.text)
}
```

```go
// old
iter := client.StreamResponses(ctx, StreamParams{Model: "redwood/text-compact", Cursor: cursor})
for iter.HasNext() {
    fmt.Println(iter.Next().Text)
}

// new
iter := client.StreamResponses(ctx, StreamParams{Model: "redwood/text-compact", ResumeToken: cursor})
for iter.HasNext() {
    fmt.Println(iter.Next().Text)
}
```


 alex: Thanks — adding a short note to the migration guide about the alias would be great. Can we also include a one-liner showing how older SDKs can still work? e.g. server side maps `cursor` -> `resume_token` for now. 


 tom: Yep, I'll add a compatibility snippet:
```py
# compatibility shim on user side
if hasattr(params, 'cursor') and not hasattr(params, 'resume_token'):
    params.resume_token = params.cursor
```


 maya: Awesome. Can you target the docs repo and mention the sample files: quickstarts/streaming/{py,ts,go}. Also please include a short test that exercises a resume token in the code-snippet harness. 


 tom: Will do. I'll open a PR in ~30m: redwood-inference/docs#xxxx with the sample edits + migration note + one unit snippet test. cc @alex for review. :shipit: 


 docs-bot: Preview build created: https://staging-docs.redwood.ai/builds/8793 — contains updated quickstart pages. 


 ci-bot: Heads-up: docs build failed on the snippet-checker step (flake: missing newline in ts example). Truncated log: "ERROR: snippet-checker.ts: line 42: expected trailing newline". 


